<!--
  CLUB CONFIG — rasa.orchestrator.soccer.club
  ===========================================

  This file is the club's PROFILE + the cross-cutting DIMENSIONS the whole
  platform reads. It is the single source of truth for WHO this club is and
  for the taxonomy every other record validates against.

  INSTALL POSTURE
  ---------------
  This template ships at `seed/club.md.template` and installs ONCE to
  `state/club.md` in the club's umbrella repo (policy: skip-if-exists). After
  install it is PROJECT-OWNED — the club director fills it and owns it forever.
  bin/init never overwrites it on upgrade. (Unlike the Element-owned
  `state/<entity>/_template.md` record templates, which ARE refreshed on
  upgrade, this is your config — yours to edit.) A director fills it once,
  then revises it as the club grows (adds an age group, a new season, a
  registration org).

  WHY IT'S LOAD-BEARING
  ---------------------
  Every skill that touches a member, a team, or a tryout VALIDATES against the
  dimensions declared here:
    - `/member`, `/team`, `/tryout` reject any `age_group` not in `#age_groups`
      and any `gender` not in `#genders`. The grid is what makes "U13 isn't a
      thing at this club" an enforceable fact instead of a typo.
    - `/status` computes its age_group × gender cross-tab and its empty-cell
      gap report against THIS catalog — that's how a cell with no team is even
      detectable.
    - `registrations[]` on members + the (phase-2) Registration entity draw
      their system names from `#registration_systems`.
  So: if a value isn't declared here, it doesn't exist to the platform. Add the
  dimension HERE first, then use it in records. Do not invent dimensions inside
  a record.

  REFERENCE SYNTAX
  ----------------
  Skills cite these dimensions as `state/club.md#age_groups`,
  `state/club.md#genders`, `state/club.md#registration_systems`. The anchors
  are the YAML keys in the frontmatter below — keep their names exact.

  FOUNDATION vs PHASE 2
  ---------------------
  - FOUNDATION (used by this build's skills): identity, age_groups, genders,
    registration_systems, seasons.
  - PHASE 2 (declared here as a placeholder, no skills authored this build):
    complexes/fields. The shape is sketched below so the catalog is ready when
    `/complex` + `/field` ship; until then leave it as the starter or remove it.

  Replace every <PLACEHOLDER>. Lists are EDITABLE — the defaults below are a
  sensible US youth-soccer starting point, not a mandate. Trim, extend, rename
  to match your club. Delete this comment block once you've filled it in.
-->

---
# ─── machine-readable: the dimensions every skill validates against ───
# Keep these YAML keys' names EXACT — skills reference them by anchor
# (state/club.md#age_groups, #genders, #registration_systems).

# ── club identity (the profile) ──
club:
  name: "<Club Name>"                 # display name. e.g. "Riverside United SC". used in /status headlines.
  short_name: "<CLUB>"                # short tag for ids/labels. e.g. "RUSC".
  founded: "<YYYY>"                   # year founded, or blank.
  location: "<City, State>"          # primary city/region the club operates in.
  governing_body: "<state assoc.>"   # the state/national association the club affiliates under (free text; see registration_systems below).
  website: "<https://example.org|>"
  primary_contact:                    # the club's main administrative contact.
    name: "<Director Name>"
    email: "<admin@example.org>"
    phone: "<+1-555-0100>"

# ── DIMENSION: age_groups ──────────────────────────────────────────────
# The club's youth-soccer age ladder. Skills validate every record's
# `age_group` against this list. EDITABLE — the default is a standard US
# youth ladder; trim or extend to your club's actual offerings. Each value
# is the literal string used in records (Member.age_group, Team.age_group,
# Tryout.age_group). Keep them short + stable (e.g. "U12", not "Under-12s").
age_groups:
  - U6                                # micro / academy
  - U8
  - U10
  - U12
  - U14
  - U16
  - U19                               # high-school age
  - Adult                             # adult / senior side, if the club fields one

# ── DIMENSION: genders ─────────────────────────────────────────────────
# The gender categories the club fields teams in. Skills validate every
# record's `gender` against this list. EDITABLE — drop `coed` if you never
# field mixed sides; some clubs prefer different labels. The default set
# covers the common youth-soccer case.
genders:
  - boys
  - girls
  - coed                              # mixed; remove if the club separates strictly

# ── DIMENSION: registration_systems ────────────────────────────────────
# Every org a member or team registers WITH, across the four levels:
# the club's own system + state / regional / national bodies. Members'
# `registrations[]` (and the phase-2 Registration entity) draw their
# `system` names from the `name` fields here. EDITABLE — fill in the real
# orgs your club registers under; the entries below are SHAPE + examples.
# `level` is one of: club | state | regional | national.
registration_systems:
  - name: "<club-system>"             # the club's own internal registration. e.g. "RUSC Registration".
    level: club
    notes: "<the club's own member/team enrollment system of record>"
  - name: "<State Soccer Association>" # e.g. a US state youth-soccer association.
    level: state
    notes: "<state-level sanctioning / player registration org>"
  - name: "<Regional League/Conference>" # e.g. a regional competitive league the club enters teams into.
    level: regional
    notes: "<regional competition body — optional; remove if not applicable>"
  - name: "<National Body>"           # e.g. a national youth-soccer organization.
    level: national
    notes: "<national affiliation / sanctioning body>"

# ── DIMENSION: seasons ─────────────────────────────────────────────────
# How the club's calendar is sliced. Team.season + Tryout dates resolve
# against this. EDITABLE — a club may run fall/spring, a single year-round
# season, or a custom split. `current` names the active season /status
# reports on by default.
seasons:
  model: "<fall-spring|year-round|custom>"   # the club's season structure.
  current: "<Fall 2026>"                      # the active season; /status defaults to this.
  list:                                       # the seasons the club runs. each is a label used in Team.season.
    - "Fall 2026"
    - "Spring 2027"
    # year-round clubs may carry a single rolling entry, e.g. "2026-27".

# ── DIMENSION: complexes / fields (PHASE 2 — placeholder) ──────────────
# The club's physical venues. PHASE 2: no `/complex` or `/field` skill is
# authored in this build, and there is no `state/complexes/` record yet.
# This block is a forward-declaration so Team.home_complex + Tryout.location
# have something to point at later. For now it is a STARTER LIST — fill in
# the names you know, or remove the block until the phase-2 skills ship.
# When they ship, each complex becomes its own `state/complexes/<id>.md`
# record (with fields[], parking, vending, address) and this list is
# superseded by that directory.
complexes:                            # PHASE 2 — declarative only this build
  - id: "<north-fields>"             # stable slug; becomes the Complex record id in phase 2.
    name: "<North Fields Complex>"
    address: "<street, city, state>"
    fields:                           # the playable fields at this complex (phase 2: each becomes a Field record).
      - id: "<north-1>"
        name: "<Field 1>"
        surface: "<grass|turf>"
        size: "<full|9v9|7v7|small-sided>"
    parking: "<notes — lots, capacity, overflow>"
    vending: "<notes — concessions, restrooms, amenities>"
---

# <Club Name> — Club Profile & Dimensions

> **<Club Name>** (`<short_name>`) · <City, State> · founded <YYYY>
> Active season: **<current season>** · governing body: <state assoc.>

This is the club's identity card and the **dimension catalog** the whole
platform reads. The frontmatter above is the machine-readable source of
truth; the sections below are the human-readable companion. Keep them in
sync — when you edit a dimension, update both the YAML and the prose.

---

## Identity *(human-authored — you own this)*

One paragraph on the club: who you are, what you field, your mission, your
competitive level (recreational / select / competitive / academy), the
community you serve. `/status` shows the `club.name`; everything else here is
context for whoever opens the repo.

- <e.g. "Riverside United SC is a community youth-soccer club fielding
   recreational and select sides U6 through U19 across the Riverside metro,
   founded 2014, affiliated through the State Youth Soccer Association.">

---

## Dimensions *(the catalog every skill validates against)*

The cross-cutting taxonomy. **This is load-bearing**: a record can only use a
value declared here. To add a U13 group, a new gender label, or a national
registration org, **edit the frontmatter list first**, then use the value.

### Age groups *(`#age_groups`)*

The club's age ladder. `/member`, `/team`, `/tryout` reject any `age_group`
not in this list; `/status` builds its age_group × gender grid from it.

> Default ladder: U6 · U8 · U10 · U12 · U14 · U16 · U19 · Adult — **editable**.
> Trim to what you actually field; add intermediate groups (U11, U13, U15,
> U17, U18) if your league uses single-year banding.

### Genders *(`#genders`)*

The categories you field sides in: `boys` · `girls` · `coed`. **Editable** —
drop `coed` if you separate strictly. `/team` and `/tryout` accept only these.

### Registration systems *(`#registration_systems`)*

The four-level enrollment picture: the club's own system + the state, regional,
and national bodies you register members and teams with. Members'
`registrations[]` use the `name` values here; the phase-2 Registration entity
(`member|team × system × season`) will resolve against this list. Fill in your
real orgs — the defaults are shape placeholders.

| Level | System (`name`) | What it's for |
|---|---|---|
| club | `<club-system>` | the club's own enrollment system of record |
| state | `<State Soccer Association>` | state-level sanctioning / player registration |
| regional | `<Regional League/Conference>` | regional competition entry (optional) |
| national | `<National Body>` | national affiliation / sanctioning |

### Seasons *(`#seasons`)*

How the calendar is sliced (`model`), the active season (`current`, what
`/status` defaults to), and the `list` of season labels `Team.season` uses.
**Editable** — fall/spring, year-round, or custom.

---

## Complexes & fields *(PHASE 2 — placeholder)*

The club's physical venues, where teams practice/play and tryouts run.

**Phase 2.** No `/complex` or `/field` skill is authored in this build and
there is no `state/complexes/` directory yet. The `complexes:` block in the
frontmatter is a **forward-declaration** so `Team.home_complex` and
`Tryout.location` have stable ids to point at — they are recorded as intent and
degrade gracefully today. When the phase-2 skills ship, each complex becomes
its own `state/complexes/<id>.md` record (carrying `fields[]`, `parking`,
`vending`, `address`), each field a `state/fields/<id>.md`, and this starter
list is superseded by those directories.

Until then: fill in the venues you know (so the references resolve to *names*),
or remove the block entirely — nothing in this build's foundation depends on it.

---

## Notes *(human-authored — preserved)*

Anything about the club that isn't a structured dimension: history, board
composition, fee structure, scholarship policy, the date you switched state
associations, the reason you renamed an age group. Free-form; yours.

- <e.g. "Added the Adult side in '25; coed only at U6–U8 per league rule;
   regional league entry is new for Fall '26.">

